  {
    "episode_id": 51127,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51127.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "You're absolutely. And so the banking committee assignment became a top priority and then looking at and understanding the need for regulatory relief and where the best opportunity was to provide that relief. And the only thing that I can say is nothing happens here unless you work in a bipartisan way. And that was perfectly obvious. But then I also had the advantage of a great bipartisan example. in what was the Warner, Corker Bell, Corker Warner, on GSE reform, and then which later became after a series of hearings, Johnson Crapo. And so I watched that process of how support for that GSE reform, now we didn't get it done, but how support was built in a bipartisan way and said, that's how you legislate in this tunnel. I really credit Bob Corker and Mark Warner with providing such an excellent example that really led to my ability to be successful as a legislator and getting things done.",
