  {
    "episode_id": 51127,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51127.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Well, I thought we picked a line where most of the regional banks would fall under, not the super regionals. I think they felt a little left behind, but a lot of them are bumping up into that major category anyway. We thought it was an appropriate line drawing. And the important thing to know about the 250 is we did not eliminate the regulator's ability to bring them back in. So if they see systemic behavior that could create systemic risk in those smaller institutions. they can always bring them back in. It's a matter of opt-in or opt-out, and the Fed can bring them back in. So when we got the argument about country-wide, for instance, we would say, well, in an examination or a stress test, if you saw things that would make you concerned, you can bring them back in, but you're going to have to have a proof point to do it. The only thing we did was move the assumption. Is that anything below 50? No, it's anything below 250. We're not going to have the application.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
