  {
    "episode_id": 51127,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51127.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think that if we could go to Mitch and say, look, this is a bill that we think we can get done a good bipartisan bill. And you'll have to work through the amendment process, but at the end of the day, it's got 60 votes in its present form. I think it's something niche would be interested in doing. I think the majority leader is always looking for those opportunities to move a bipartisan bill, whether it's a farm bill, whether it's 2155. We're moving in a pretty rapid pace on appropriations bills. So I'd have to say that in the last, since 2155, we have seen more bipartisan bills moving forward.",
