  },
  {
    "episode_id": 51127,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51127.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "I have had that conversation with my colleagues only to have that conversation cut short very rapidly. And so one of the reasons why you didn't see the Consumer Finance Protection Bureau in 2155 was that this is such a, it's become such a political issue where I think consumer protection should never be a political issue. We should all agree on it. I think on top of that is the financing of it, whether it should be done through the appropriations process. I think we should have a meaningful debate about what that should look like going forward. One of the things that I will tell you that is discouraging to me, and probably a great example of this is the XM Bank, is that when you go to a kind of quorum-based commission, if we can't move nominees, then we can't get things done. We don't have a quorum at the XM Bank, and that's problematic, because then we can't do any credit over $10 million, which means that very large credits, we've got over $45 billion right now waiting financing. And that's just untenable. If you look at the postal commissions, I mean, I sit on very many committees where we don't have functioning quorums on commissions. And so that would concern me in trying to figure out how we could get Congress to do a bison consent the way it should do, or the Senate, so that we can, in fact, get quorums. You know, I guess politics is the art of the possible. And I think these kinds of things, in spite of kind of the look back that you just gave me, I think that even now it would not be possible to come to a bipartisan conclusion on what should happen.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "I have had conversations with my colleagues that were abruptly ended.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "A situation with $45 billion in unfinanced credit is untenable.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Without a quorum at the XM Bank, no credit over $10 million can be approved.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "The XM Bank lacks a quorum.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "Over $45 billion in credit is currently awaiting financing due to lack of quorum.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "Consumer protection should not be a political issue.",
