    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51127.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "Well, I support it. Obviously, Corker Warner, I was one of the sponsors. Like I said, I think a lot of people thought that we created something that was too complicated. Not sure I'm convinced that that's true. There's some discussion about breaking this into much smaller institutions that would be more competitive. And, you know, wouldn't be putting all your eggs in one or two baskets. I'm not sure. I know that. I think that what we really need to do is have a high level discussion about what are the risks that we're taking? How can we fix those risks and sit down with people who have been doing this for years? and say what makes sense. And then, as I said, politics is the art of the possible. I think that housing reform or GSE reform and affordable housing have to be for next Congress's banking committee, the top priority.",
