  {
    "episode_id": 51127,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51127.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 51,
    "turn_text": "Well, it's hard. I mean, we've had a couple harsh committee hearings with them, both on the false accounts that were opened and then, you know, taking a look at the insurance problems that they had. You know, at some point you say, you know, you just can't keep coming and saying, I didn't know. And one of the resistance points that I have is that they did know on the accounts And the question is, what are you doing in response to these problems? Now, they are a very large institution and organization. But again, it's not going to sell with me to say it's all my employees' fault and we're a large organization. I would argue that they created a culture that resulted in a lot of the challenges that they have right now, incentivizing opening of new accounts or punishing people who didn't open up enough new accounts. So I think as this true of any organization, their size, there's going to be challenges, but they need to have a level of accountability that reflects the challenges that we're seeing right now. And, you know, the corporate board, how many times can you say we're on it? You know, before you say, look, you know, is there anything else?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
